  "entry": "E028",
  "article": "Nvidia Launches GPU Backstop Financing Model, Takes Cut of Cloud Revenue From Neocloud Partners",
  "gold_statement": "is deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with Nvidia",
  "gold_meaning": {
   "who": "Sharon AI",
   "what": "GB300 deployment in Australia under a six-year agreement with NVIDIA (first adopter)",
   "how_much": "up to 40,000 GPUs",
   "period": "six years",
   "status": "plan"
  },
  "draws": {
   "A1": [
    "Nvidia on July 1 unveiled a new financing vehicle it calls the \"AI Compute Partnership,\" under which the chipmaker acts as a financial backstop for neocloud customers' GPU deployments and, in return, takes a recurring share of the cloud revenue those GPUs generate [1] .",
    "The program's first two adopters are Sharon AI (NASDAQ: SHAZ), an Australian sovereign-cloud provider planning up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs, and Firmus Technologies, which is building a 360MW campus in Batam, Indonesia, targeting up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs [1] [2] .",
    "Nvidia described the model as providing \"economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model\" in a blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress [1] [3] .",
    "The specific revenue-share percentage was not disclosed, and Nvidia declined to offer further details beyond the blog post [3] .",
    "The backstop mechanism works by Nvidia agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate, effectively de-risking lender exposure and making it easier for smaller cloud operators to secure capital for large GPU deployments [1] [3] .",
    "Under the AI Compute Partnership, Nvidia guarantees a floor utilization rate on deployed GPUs. If a neocloud partner's customer demand falls short, Nvidia commits to renting the idle capacity at a predetermined rate, absorbing the downside risk that would otherwise sit with lenders or equity investors [1] [3] .",
    "The company framed the program as accelerating 'adoption of Nvidia platforms among the high-growth, high-conviction AI native sector' [1] .",
    "Sharon AI, which listed on the Nasdaq in February 2026 via a $125 million IPO, is deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with Nvidia [2] [6] .",
    "Firmus Technologies, a private company, is constructing a campus in Batam, Indonesia, built to Nvidia's DGX SuperPOD (DSX) reference architecture specifications. The facility is expected to scale to 360MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs [1] [3] ."
   ],
   "A2": [
