  "entry": "E036",
  "article": "Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why",
  "gold_statement": "The bank estimates Nvidia will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when sold in volume.",
  "gold_meaning": {
   "who": "Morgan Stanley Research (an estimate)",
   "what": "NVIDIA's selling price per Rubin GPU and per Vera CPU",
   "how_much": "about $55,000 per GPU; $5,000 per CPU",
   "status": "forecast"
  },
  "draws": {
   "A1": [
    "Morgan Stanley Research estimates that Nvidia 's Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million per unit, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation.",
    "Morgan Stanley puts memory content per rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage that was virtually absent from earlier systems.",
    "As a share of the bill of materials, memory rose from 5 to 10 percent on the GB200 to 25 to 30 percent on the VR200, while the GPU's share fell from roughly 63 percent to 51 percent.",
    "First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.",
    "Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the rack price down to around $6.7 million, a reminder that procurement structure now materially moves the number."
