A1,A2,A3,B3 The backstop mechanism works by Nvidia agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate, effectively de-risking lender exposure and making it easier for smaller cloud operators to secure capital for large GPU deployments [1] [3] .
A1,A2,A3,B3 Under the AI Compute Partnership, Nvidia guarantees a floor utilization rate on deployed GPUs. If a neocloud partner's customer demand falls short, Nvidia commits to renting the idle capacity at a predetermined rate, absorbing the downside risk that would otherwise sit with lenders or equity investors [1] [3] .
A1 The company framed the program as accelerating 'adoption of Nvidia platforms among the high-growth, high-conviction AI native sector' [1] .
